# Personal data stays out of the public repo — see CLAUDE.md.
# Store, venue, group and kit profiles and the standing menu all live in
# ../event-prep-private/. These patterns are a backstop, not the rule: the rule
# is that personal data is never written here in the first place.
#
# Deliberately broad. The narrow version of this list (private/, *-sourcing.md)
# would have let venue-notes-private.md, sourcing-notes.md or a .env through on
# a `git add .` — see finding 11 on why enumerated coverage is the weak kind.
private/
*private*
*-sourcing.md
*sourcing*
kit-inventory*
standing-menu*
.env
.env.*

# Session transcripts. They contain whatever was discussed — real prices, what
# people paid, phone numbers — so they live in ../event-prep-private/transcripts/.
# Write up the lessons in docs/PHASE-0-FINDINGS.md instead. Covers exports in
# other formats, not just the .jsonl they arrive as.
*.jsonl
transcripts/
*transcript*

